{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"16 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,50.531,3.651,3.268,"Tata Motors Passenger Vehicles"],[13.889,14.731,32.802,2.373,2.124,"Cheap only on consensus earnings"],[13.889,20.845,52.934,1.809,1.634,"Tata Motors PV fell 8.7% today to ₹262.40, near its 52-week low, after Friday’s"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Q2 FY27 results cut JLR’s guidance five months after it was set. We rate the"],[13.889,23.733,52.931,1.809,1.634,"shares Neutral with a Dec-27 target of ₹275. They look cheap at 0.9x book and"],[13.889,25.177,52.931,1.809,1.634,"6.7x consensus FY28E EPS, but our FY28E EPS of ₹18.77 is about half the"],[13.889,26.621,52.928,1.809,1.634,"consensus ₹39.03. Today’s price implies a JLR earning a 4.3% long-run EBIT"],[13.889,28.065,34.783,1.809,1.634,"margin, against 2.0% in H1 FY27 and 8.5% in FY25."],[13.889,30.551,52.936,1.809,1.634,"The 34% rise in Q2 revenue was measured against last year’s cyber-incident"],[13.889,31.995,52.951,1.809,1.634,"quarter. JLR’s EBIT margin fell to 1.1% from 2.8% in Q1. Its FY27 guidance,"],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"set in June at about 4% EBIT and breakeven cash flow, is now 2-3% and an"],[13.889,34.883,52.959,1.809,1.634,"outflow of about £1.25bn. Profit also leans on capitalised spending: JLR"],[13.889,36.328,52.931,1.809,1.634,"capitalised £932m of engineering in H1 against £624m of depreciation and"],[13.889,37.772,52.934,1.809,1.634,"amortisation, and the group holds ₹87,574 cr of intangible assets under"],[13.889,39.216,52.957,1.809,1.634,"development, 91% of its market value, which begin to amortise as the new"],[13.889,40.684,52.936,1.809,1.634,"electric models reach customers from early 2027. In India revenue rose 51%, yet"],[13.889,42.128,52.951,1.809,1.634,"the EBITDA margin was 4.0%, of which 2.9 points were government incentives,"],[13.889,43.572,23.233,1.809,1.634,"mostly PLI, which ends with FY28."],[13.889,46.034,52.936,1.809,1.634,"Our target averages two sum-of-the-parts values. On earnings multiples (JLR at"],[13.889,47.502,52.931,1.809,1.634,"7.1x, the median forward P/E of BMW, Mercedes-Benz, Porsche and Volvo"],[13.889,48.946,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Car; Tata PV at 22.7x, the median of Maruti, M&M and Hyundai India) the"],[13.889,50.39,52.928,1.809,1.634,"shares are worth ₹243. On discounted cash flows, with JLR’s long-run EBIT"],[13.889,51.834,52.931,1.809,1.634,"margin at 5%, they are worth ₹308; each point of that margin moves the value"],[13.889,53.278,52.988,1.809,1.634,"by about ₹63. Upside risks: JLR meets its FY28 aim of double-digit EBITDA"],[13.889,54.722,52.951,1.809,1.634,"and positive cash flow, or PLI is extended. Downside risks: China, US tariffs,"],[13.889,56.167,52.931,1.809,1.634,"slow orders for the electric models, and net debt, which we see rising to ₹55,700"],[13.889,57.611,41.156,1.809,1.634,"cr by March 2028 where management expects a peak this year."],[13.889,60.098,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.268,67.952,1.489,1.022,0.915,"250"],[15.268,65.843,1.489,1.022,0.915,"300"],[15.268,63.746,1.489,1.022,0.915,"350"],[15.268,61.639,1.489,1.022,0.915,"400"],[18.224,68.646,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.848,68.646,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.635,68.646,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.391,68.646,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.714,69.817,3.091,1.275,1.111,"TMPV ("],[21.808,69.843,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.421,69.817,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.505,69.817,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.285,70.977,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.556,70.977,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.276,70.977,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,70.977,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,72.043,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[18.784,72.043,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−28.0%"],[24.055,72.043,2.842,1.387,1.209,"−8.5%"],[28.224,72.043,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−21.6%"],[32